cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "Learning art by names or by looking: how the training signal reshapes a vision model's view of art"
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: "Sitani"
    given-names: "Divya"
    affiliation: "Independent Researcher"
repository-code: "https://github.com/Divya1205/art-training-vision-models"
abstract: >
  Code for a controlled comparison of two ways of further training
  pretrained vision models (DINOv2-small and DINOv3-small) on 960
  WikiArt paintings from eight styles: labels (predicting each
  painting's style) and exposure (a contrastive objective with no
  style names). One notebook trains all conditions and computes every
  result: style accessibility and presence probes, style organisation,
  the abstract-versus-representational distance with painting-level
  and spread-controlled measures, controls, exact null tests and
  image-statistics checks. No images are redistributed; paintings are
  loaded from the public huggan/wikiart dataset at run time.
keywords:
  - representation-learning
  - vision-transformers
  - self-supervised-learning
  - contrastive-learning
  - probing
  - art-perception
  - expertise
  - neuroaesthetics
license: MIT
date-released: 2026-11-18
version: 0.1.0
